Q: Extending class and assigning different value to an existing property A: <p>The parent's type annotation only applies to the parent's own assignments, not to the child's.</p>
<p>Typescript doesn't inherit the JSDoc type annotation to child classes automatically.</p>
<p>Typescript limitation actually, not issue with your understanding.</p>
<p>So, re-annotate will fix.</p>
<pre><code>class X {
    constructor() {
        /** @type {'a'|'b'|'c'} */
        this.property = 'a';
    }
}

class Y extends X {
    constructor() {
        super();

        /** @type {'a'|'b'|'c'} */
        this.property = 'b';
    }
}
</code></pre>
